B.a0d=s(["Digestive System: Pepsin breaks down proteins in stomach (pH ~1.5); Amylase digests carbohydrates in saliva; Bile (produced in liver, stored in gallbladder) emulsifies fats.","Circulatory System: Humans have a four-chambered heart with complete double circulation. Normal blood pressure is 120/80 mm Hg.","Blood Components: RBCs (erythrocytes, carry oxygen via hemoglobin, lifespan 120 days); WBCs (leukocytes, immune defense); Platelets (blood clotting).",'Endocrine Glands: Pituitary ("Master Gland" secretes Growth Hormone, TSH); Thyroid (secretes Thyroxine, requires Iodine); Pancreas (Islets of Langerhans secrete Insulin and Glucagon).',"Deficiency Diseases: Iodine deficiency causes Goitre; Vitamin C deficiency causes Scurvy; Iron deficiency causes Anemia."],t.s)
